# Java/Spring Code Style Rules

## Formatting
Google Java Format is the single source of truth. The Spotless Maven plugin enforces it in CI:

```xml
<plugin>
    <groupId>com.diffplug.spotless</groupId>
    <artifactId>spotless-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    <configuration>
        <java>
            <googleJavaFormat/>
        </java>
    </configuration>
</plugin>
```

Run `mvn spotless:apply` to auto-format locally. CI runs `mvn spotless:check` and fails on violations. Never submit a PR with formatting errors.

## Records for DTOs
In Java 21+, prefer records over POJO classes for DTOs:

```java
// Preferred
public record UserDto(
    @NotBlank String name,
    @Email String email
) {}

// Avoid — unnecessary boilerplate
public class UserDto {
    private String name;
    private String email;
    // getters, setters, equals, hashCode, toString...
}
```

Records are immutable, have built-in `equals`/`hashCode`/`toString`, and express intent clearly.

## Lombok Restrictions
Allowed Lombok annotations:
- `@RequiredArgsConstructor` — constructor injection
- `@Getter` — on entities/non-record classes
- `@Setter` — on entities when needed
- `@Builder` — for complex object construction
- `@Slf4j` — logging

Forbidden on `@Entity` classes:
- `@Data` — causes Hibernate issues (infinite recursion in `hashCode`/`equals` via bidirectional relationships)
- `@EqualsAndHashCode` — use natural key or `@Id` for entity equality instead

## No `Optional` as Method Parameters
`Optional` is a return type only. Never use it as a parameter:

```java
// Correct
Optional<User> findByEmail(String email);

// Forbidden
void update(Optional<String> name); // callers should not pass Optional
```

## Package Structure by Feature
Group code by feature/domain, not by layer. This makes the codebase navigable and makes extracting a feature into its own service trivial:

```
src/main/java/com/example/app/
    users/                         ← everything related to users
        UserController.java
        UserService.java
        UserRepository.java
        User.java
        UserDto.java
        UserMapper.java
    orders/                        ← everything related to orders
        OrderController.java
        ...
    shared/                        ← cross-cutting concerns
        GlobalExceptionHandler.java
        ErrorResponse.java
```

Do not use `controllers/`, `services/`, `repositories/` as top-level packages.
